  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read this page",
      "items": [
        "Product quality map asks what behavior matters and which assurance mechanism belongs at each product boundary.",
        "Evaluation runtime shows the reusable engineering machinery that executes cases, grades outputs, persists runs, compares baseline/candidate, and applies gates."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "1 · Reproducible run identity",
      "items": [
        "Dataset fingerprint, subject configuration and code/dependency provenance are separate contracts.",
        "A completed run records terminal per-case observations; completion does not mean every case passed."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "emerald",
      "title": "2 · Pair the same cases",
      "items": [
        "Baseline and candidate must use the exact same dataset snapshot and case IDs.",
        "Pass→fail/error is a regression; fail/error→pass is an improvement; case evidence remains visible."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "violet",
      "title": "3 · Uncertainty without pretending tiny sets are enough",
      "items": [
        "Shared numeric dimensions are compared as paired candidate-minus-baseline case deltas.",
        "Paired-bootstrap intervals are withheld below 20 pairs by default; QE-108 supplies the larger benchmark."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "4 · Hard invariants differ from decision metrics",
      "items": [
        "Hard invariants require every candidate score to exist and explicitly pass.",
        "Decision metrics compare mean movement with an allowed regression budget; QE-110 will decide real workflow thresholds."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "5 · Workflow enforcement is now executable",
      "items": [
        "PRs execute the same synthetic development dataset against the base SHA and head SHA, then fail on case regressions, decision-metric regression, execution errors, or hard-invariant failures.",
        "The gate report records both code revisions and is uploaded with baseline/candidate run evidence instead of reducing the result to a green check."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "6 · Still not a release-quality benchmark",
      "items": [
        "The 14-case V1/growing V2 development evidence is a regression detector, not a statistically valid promotion benchmark; QE-108 adds the larger locked holdout and confidence intervals.",
        "Real-model unrelated no-answer relevance remains non-blocking until QE-109 calibrates abstention; access/currentness/integrity stay hard blockers."
      ]
    }
  ]
}
